   <platform os="all" arch="noarch" version="1.9.6:1.9.99">
      <package fileName="TGScripts_repository.tar.gz" sha1="e99dcc97be65cdb68ee6a6c6bb4bf44030068dba" type="script" releaseDate="20261115">
         <title>
            TGScripts - Astro Bucket List 0.45.0
         </title>
         <remove>
            src/scripts/TGScripts
            doc/scripts/AberrationInspectorTG
            doc/scripts/AberrationSpotterTG
            doc/scripts/AstroBucketList
            doc/scripts/BBStarReduction
            doc/scripts/ColorMaskTG
            doc/scripts/CSTG
            doc/scripts/DarkStructureEnhanceTG
            doc/scripts/DeconvolutionPreviewTG
            doc/scripts/LinearMasterBlend
            doc/scripts/LocalSupportMask
            doc/scripts/LRGBDeconvolutionMatch
            doc/scripts/ROILinearFit
            doc/scripts/StarSpikeProtectionMask
            doc/scripts/SubframeQualityReview
            doc/scripts/TGScriptSkeleton
            doc/scripts/EmissionLineIntegrationTG
            doc/scripts/TGFieldMosaic
            doc/scripts/TGCornerMosaic
            doc/scripts/TGHueRangeMask
            doc/scripts/TGDustContrast
            doc/scripts/TGPSFComparison
         </remove>
         <description>
            <p>
               Astro Bucket List 0.45.0 adds local catalog lookup, richer interactive finder charts and observing-window planning. Requires PixInsight 1.9.6 Lockhart build 1718 or later.
            </p>
            <p>
               Look up targets in configured local catalogs and use bundled nebula outlines. SIMBAD remains available for missing objects and richer information, while manually edited metadata is preserved.
            </p>
            <p>
               Finder charts use the native chart engine with the Observing Atlas style and SVG/PDF export. Automatic projection, Milky Way shading and adjustable star density, size and color provide more control over chart appearance.
            </p>
            <p>
               Inspect, select, edit or add objects from the chart; zoom, pan and navigate with Center selection, Back, Forward and Home. Save table views and named chart presets. Unified Configuration brings chart settings, details, catalogs and outlines together, with persistent preferences and consistent Apply/Cancel behavior.
            </p>
            <p>
               Plan the filtered targets for an observing site, evening date and fixed UTC offset. Compare altitude, darkness and optional Moon-separation limits, rank usable observing time and inspect target, Sun and Moon altitude curves. Calculations use local ephemerides, remain responsive and keep site preferences local.
            </p>
            <p>
               Layout refinements keep collapsible sections from resizing the window, make controls more compact and replace intrusive chart tooltips with concise status hints. Deprecated ByteArray access has been replaced. Updated documentation and a shorter README cover the current features.
            </p>
            <p>
               SIMBAD-derived object-type data now includes separate ODbL licensing, attribution and a reusable data copy. SIMBAD and DSS downloads use HTTPS and stricter size, content and decoding checks; DSS cache reuse verifies a SHA-256 digest.
            </p>
            <p>
               Copyright (c) 2026 Dr. Thorsten Glebe. All Rights Reserved.
            </p>
         </description>
      </package>
   </platform>
</xri>
